    "kg_brand_strings_excluded_reason": "none excluded: every KG brand string maps to one registry entry (case variants such as 'Hera'/'hera' and 'e.l.f.'/'elf' merge); the three fake subjects are kept as is_placeholder entries so that normalization can flag them",
    "policy": [
      "Only facts stated in a source file are recorded. Unknown group/segment/origin/acquired stay null (OE4: registry brand with null group is 'not a member'; brand outside the registry is 'unknown').",
      "origin: taken from config/brands.json (target_brand.country, amorepacific_brands[].country, competitor_brands[].country, korean_brands list, brand_ownership). The KG snapshot's originatesFrom=Korea for 30 AP brands is NOT used: it comes from the default country='Korea' in src/ontology/kg_updater.py (load_brand_ownership), not from a stated fact.",
      "segment: amorepacific_brands[].segment and competitor_brands[].tier / tracked_competitors tier, mapped to the unified vocabulary in schema.json 'segments'. config/brands.json 'segments' block disagrees with the per-brand entries for HERA (+Makeup), ETUDE (+Makeup), HOLITUAL (Health vs Wellness), OSULLOC (Lifestyle vs Tea); the per-brand entry wins and the block is not used.",
      "placeholders: unknown/fresh/chi are KG artifacts (docs/analysis/ontology-review-2026-09-18.md section 3.2).",
      "name: canonical display spelling from config files; for KG-only brands the KG spelling (cased variant if one exists, otherwise the lowercase string) until someone edits it."
    ]
  },
